## H2 — Long SECRET ident (heap vs time)
### Mechanism (code, not slogan)
`oo_char_at` (`ooda/runtime/chs_rt_str.c`):

- `utf8_byte_index` rescans from byte 0 to `idx` every call
- Always `malloc`s a 1-char `OoStr`

Needle match + ident scan: `char_at(src, ·)` over the file ⇒ **Θ(n²) time** + short-lived 1-char temps (ARC `oo_str_release` on the cursor if emit elides correctly).

`oo_str_slice(src, start, k)` is **one** span copy of the ident (plus `oo_chars_len` / two `utf8_byte_index` walks). After the fix there is **no** prefix-string chain `""`, `"A"`, `"Aa"`, …, full name.

Once-per-hit `"__sec__" + name` is O(|name|) and O(#directives), not O(|name|²) rebuild of the ident itself.

### Pre-fix binary (honesty: leak was live)
Host `oodac` is **07:49 / `a44ee35e…`**, built **before** the 11:54 source rewrite. Ephemeral `/tmp/s710_mem_*` (not landed) `emit-c` of `// SECRET: A`+`a`*(N-1) + `fn main() { println(1) }` against that **old** binary:

| Ident N | src B | sec | maxrss KB | rc |
|--------:|------:|----:|----------:|---:|
| 3 (`tok`) | 40 | 0.01 | 4464 | 0 |
| 2048 | 2085 | 2.28 | 18232 | 0 |
| 4096 | 4133 | 9.01 | 31164 | 0 |
| 8192 | 8229 | 34.17 | 58296 | 0 |

Time 2k→4k→8k ≈ 4.0× / 3.8× for 2× length — quadratic, consistent with concat + `char_at`. RSS +13–27 MB per doubling is the **old** prefix-chain / walk tax. **Do not** treat these numbers as post-fix heap.

Post-fix RSS on a rebuilt product binary is **not** measured this pass (no rebuild; not Memory Auditor OWN). Re-open 7.10 only if concat returns, or emit-c of a ≤64 KiB SECRET ident **OOMs** / walker RSS grows as Θ(n²) **after** a binary that contains L65 `str_slice`.

**H2 heap (source mechanism): PASS. H2 time: residual. H2 product-binary RSS: unproved (pre-fix host).**

